            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years and Education</strong><br>\nJames Dewey Watson was born on April 6, 1928, in Chicago, Illinois. Fascinated by bird watching as a child, his interest in genetics was spurred by reading \"What Is Life?\" by Erwin Schrödinger. He attended the University of Chicago and Indiana University for his graduate studies in zoology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Discovery of the DNA Structure</strong><br>\nIn 1953, Watson, along with Francis Crick and Maurice Wilkins, discovered the double helix structure of DNA. This groundbreaking work, conducted at the University of Cambridge, provided a visual model of DNA and won them the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine in 1962.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Career in Academia and Research</strong><br>\nWatson continued his research in molecular biology, becoming a professor and later the director of the Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory in New York. Here, he focused on the study of cancer and the regulation of cell growth.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Involvement in the Human Genome Project</strong><br>\nWatson was appointed as the first director of the Human Genome Project in 1988. His leadership helped initiate the efforts to map all the genes in the human genome, which has revolutionized biology and medicine.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Controversial Views and Public Debate</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Watson has been a figure of both scientific prominence and public controversy. His opinions on genetics and intelligence have sparked debate and criticism, overshadowing some of his scientific contributions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Books and Publications</strong><br>\nWatson's account of the discovery of DNA's structure, \"The Double Helix,\" is a famous narrative that details the human story behind the scientific breakthrough. His other books aimed to make science accessible to the public.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
